questions.question:
The checkout code (default READ COMMITTED isolation):

-- session A
BEGIN;
SELECT id, status FROM enrollments WHERE id = 42 FOR UPDATE;
-- A now calls the payment provider, which takes about 8 seconds, then:
UPDATE enrollments SET status = 'active' WHERE id = 42;
COMMIT;

-- session B, 2 seconds after A's SELECT ... FOR UPDATE
SELECT status FROM enrollments WHERE id = 42;

Statement: "Session B's query waits about 6 seconds, until A commits, because A holds a row lock on enrollment 42."
